=== p2-windows · W7 · page:analytics/Timeline (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:analytics/Timeline   kind=page   web route=/timeline
Web source  : web/src/features/analytics/pages/TimelinePage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage / SchemaDriftPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "TimelinePage.xaml +
  TimelinePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Analytics" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("Timeline", already in RouteTable.cs → /timeline) in
  Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useVehicles (GET /vehicles); the page additionally derives its
  panels from the two vehicle-states queries (GET /vehicle-states/timeline, GET /vehicle-states/summary) the web page
  runs. The view-model reads all three through an injected ITimelineFeed; the default EmptyTimelineFeed resolves the
  empty state (matching the ApiLogsPage/SchemaDriftPage host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed
  TimelineClientFeed (TimelinePage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract operations get_api_v1_vehicles
  (no params) + get_api_v1_vehicle_states_timeline / get_api_v1_vehicle_states_summary (snake_case vehicle_id + days
  query params, never camelCase, never a double /api/v1 prefix), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. No HTTP
  touches the view; non-success surfaces as ApiException -> the failure banner.
- The web page renders the failure banner (anyError) above always-present panels, a full-page loading scaffold while
  the first query is in flight with no rows, and per-region empty states; the native port reproduces them as visible
  Fluent regions per ADR-006: loading -> TsPageLoadSkeleton; error -> TsAlertBanner(Danger) (web anyError) above the
  content; distribution/daily empties -> TsChartSkeleton (while loading) / TsEmptyState; transitions empty ->
  TsEmptyState. Never a blank region.
- SI units: this surface carries no unit-bearing fields (FSM state transitions + time-in-state seconds + transition
  counts only). Durations format through the shared NumberFormatting port (web fmtInt, half-away-from-zero, verified
  by FormatDurationFromSeconds_matches_web) and timestamps through DateTimeFormatting (web formatDateTime) at the
  display boundary — no non-SI value is ever stored or computed.
- i18n: 21 of the 23 manifest keys already existed in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; the 2 missing required keys
  (timeline.noStateData, timeline.trigger — the web resolves these via inline t() fallbacks, they are absent from
  en.json) were added verbatim (web key names) to all three catalogs, plus the action-row keys timeline.range /
  timeline.range.last7Days/last30Days/last90Days / timeline.refresh. The surface resolves every literal through the
  ILocalizer facade; ar/he carry the English default until translated, matching the existing catalog convention.
- Tests link the three Microsoft.UI-free files (Model/Source/ViewModel) into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj via the
  established <Compile Include … Link="FeatureViews\TimelinePage\…"> convention (the headless test assembly cannot
  reference the WinUI exe); the bare WinUI view (TimelinePage.cs) is excluded (it uses Microsoft.UI).

